<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zimri (king of Israel)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 885 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zimri was king of Israel for seven days around 885 BCE, according to the Bible. A commander of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a>, he killed King Elah and his family at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirzah">Tirzah</a>, but the army proclaimed its general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a> king and besieged the city. Zimri burned the royal palace over himself, and Omri emerged from the civil war that followed as the founder of a new dynasty.</p></div>
